From 72db05ff958ecdc8322f3c1f2a0d8572f83b17de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:10:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 059/110] ASoC: codecs: sc2723: use pmdown_time

Without use_pmdown_time in any component of the link, ASoC powers the
path down as soon as a stream closes, so every new sound switched the
speaker PA on again. The PA pops at every switch, on and off; the clocks,
DACs, AOL and the PA supply switch silently (checked step by step), and
neither the PA soft start bits nor class D mode avoid it.

With the default 5 s delay short gaps no longer pop. Userspace can set
pmdown_time to -1 to keep the path up until system suspend: the speaker
path at idle draws less than about 0.5 mA, below what the fuel gauge
resolves.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/sc2723-codec.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/sc2723-codec.c b/sound/soc/codecs/sc2723-codec.c
index 9b9c491c6..bb9454484 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/sc2723-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/sc2723-codec.c
@@ -283,6 +283,7 @@ static const struct snd_soc_component_driver sc2723_codec_driver = {
 	.dapm_routes = sc2723_dapm_routes,
 	.num_dapm_routes = ARRAY_SIZE(sc2723_dapm_routes),
 	.idle_bias_on = false,
+	.use_pmdown_time = true,
 	.endianness = 1,
 };
 
